    "text": "<p>From the top&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;of a vertical wall&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;of height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the angles of depression of the top&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;and bottom&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;of a vertical tower&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>15</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>60</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup></math> respectively,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;are on the same horizontal level. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is a point on&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">,</mo></math> then the area (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>) of the quadrilateral&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to</p>",
